**API v2 — GraphQL retry after JWT refresh**

**Paginated reads.** When a JWT expires between pages, refresh the token and replay the query with the **same `after` cursor** you used on the failed request — that is, the `endCursor` returned by the last successful page. Do not advance the cursor and do not restart from page 1.

```graphql
query ListWorkspaces($first: Int!, $after: String) {
  workspaces(first: $first, after: $after) {
    nodes { id name }
    pageInfo { hasNextPage endCursor }
  }
}

# Page 1 returned endCursor "cD0yMDI0...".
# Page 2 returned 401 AuthExpiredError -> refresh JWT, then replay:
#   $after = "cD0yMDI0..."   (unchanged)
```

**Mutations.** An `AuthExpiredError` returned before the resolver runs means the server did not execute the mutation. After refreshing the JWT, retry the exact same operation. There is no server-side state to roll back and no client-side dedupe token is required.

```graphql
mutation CreateWorkspace($input: CreateWorkspaceInput!) {
  createWorkspace(input: $input) { workspace { id } }
}

# 401 AuthExpiredError before resolver -> safe to retry identically after refresh.
```

**Token rotation.** Refresh the JWT and resend the same `X-Scaffold-Workspace` + `X-Scaffold-Signature` headers. API v2 has no separate token-rotation header.

